":"Without in-loop validation, you get JSON that may or may not match your schema. You then have to write error handling, decide whether to retry, and figure out how to feed errors back."},"1147":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-10","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#why-validation-inside-the-loop","content":"Struktur does all of this for you."},"1148":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-11","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-the-retry-loop-works","content":"Send the extraction prompt to the LLM."},"1149":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-12","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-the-retry-loop-works","content":"Validate the response against the schema."},"1150":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-13","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-the-retry-loop-works","content":"If valid: return it."},"1151":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-14","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-the-retry-loop-works","content":"If invalid: serialize the validation errors into an XML block, append it to the message thread as a user message, go to step 1."},"1152":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-15","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-the-retry-loop-works","content":"After `maxAttempts` (default 3): throw."},"1153":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-16","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-the-retry-loop-works","content":"The model sees its own mistake and a structured description of it. This self-correction loop is why most extractions converge within 2 attempts."},"1154":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-17","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#schema-design-affects-retry-rate","content":"Well-constrained schemas fail less often. Tips:"},"1155":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-18","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#schema-design-affects-retry-rate","content":"Always use `additionalProperties: false`."},"1156":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-19","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#schema-design-affects-retry-rate","content":"Use `required` arrays explicitly."},"1157":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-20","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#schema-design-affects-retry-rate","content":"Prefer `enum` for categorical fields."},"1158":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-21","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#schema-design-affects-retry-rate","content":"Use `format` (e.g., `date`, `email`) only when you need it — it adds validation surface."},"1159":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-22","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#observing-retries-with-events","content":"Use the `onMessage` event to see when retries happen:"},"1160":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-23","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#smart-validation-for-multi-step-strategies","content":"When using parallel or sequential strategies, your data might be split across multiple chunks. For example, an invoice's price might appear on page 1, while the vendor name appears on page 5. If both fields are `required` in your schema, validating intermediate results would fail unnecessarily."},"1161":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-24","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"Struktur uses **lenient validation** during intermediate extraction steps:"},"1162":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-25","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"**Type errors** (`string` vs `number`) → Retry immediately"},"1163":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-26","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"**Format errors** (invalid email) → Retry immediately"},"1164":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-27","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"**Required field errors** → Allowed during intermediate steps"},"1165":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-28","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"**All constraints** → Enforced on final validation"},"1166":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-29","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"This means the model can extract partial data without pressure to hallucinate missing required fields. The final validation ensures all required fields are present before returning."},"1167":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-30","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#opting-into-strict-validation","content":"Disable smart validation with the `strict` flag:"},"1168":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-31","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#opting-into-strict-validation","content":"Use `strict: true` when:"},"1169":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-32","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#opting-into-strict-validation","content":"You know each chunk contains complete data"},"1170":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-33","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#opting-into-strict-validation","content":"You want early failure on missing fields"},"1171":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-34","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#opting-into-strict-validation","content":"You're debugging extraction issues"},"1172":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-35","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#see-also","content":"The Extraction Pipeline — where validation fits"},"1173":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-36","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#see-also","content":"Events & Observability — the events API"},"1174":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-37","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#see-also","content":"The Artifact Format — schema format"},"1175":{"id":"/docs","page_id":"/docs","type":"page","content":"What is Struktur?","breadcrumbs":["Struktur"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs"},"1176":{"id":"/docs-0","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"All-in-one tool for structured data extraction using an autonomous agent that turns documents into validated JSON."},"1177":{"id":"/docs-1","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#why-struktur","content":"Why Struktur?"},"1178":{"id":"/docs-2","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#why-an-agent","content":"Why an Agent?"},"1179":{"id":"/docs-3","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#why-not-managed-apis","content":"Why not managed APIs?"},"1180":{"id":"/docs-4","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#why-not-a-plain-llm-sdk-call","content":"Why not a plain LLM SDK call?"},"1181":{"id":"/docs-5","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#design-philosophy","content":"Design philosophy"},"1182":{"id":"/docs-6","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#trade-offs","content":"Trade-offs"},"1183":{"id":"/docs-7","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#a-10-second-demo","content":"A 10-second demo"},"1184":{"id":"/docs-8","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#what-struktur-is-not","content":"What Struktur is NOT"},"1185":{"id":"/docs-9","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#who-is-it-for","content":"Who is it for?"},"1186":{"id":"/docs-10","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#what-is-the-agent-strategy","content":"What is the Agent Strategy?"},"1187":{"id":"/docs-11","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"1188":{"id":"/docs-12","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#when-to-use-other-strategies","content":"When to use other strategies"},"1189":{"id":"/docs-13","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#quick-navigation","content":"Quick navigation"},"1190":{"id":"/docs-14","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"Struktur is an all-in-one tool for structured data extraction using an **autonomous agent**. It turns documents into validated, schema-typed JSON by having an LLM agent explore the content, decide what to read, and build the output incrementally."},"1191":{"id":"/docs-15","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"CLI Tool\" description=\"Extract data from the command line with a simple, intuitive interface\" href=\"/docs/cli\" />"},"1192":{"id":"/docs-16","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"TypeScript SDK\" description=\"Programmatic API for embedding extraction in your applications\" href=\"/docs/sdk\" />"},"1193":{"id":"/docs-17","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Agent Strategy\" description=\"Autonomous exploration with virtual filesystem tools\" href=\"/docs/explanation/strategies#agent\" />"},"1194":{"id":"/docs-18","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Examples\" description=\"Real-world extraction patterns and use cases\" href=\"/docs/examples\" />"},"1195":{"id":"/docs-19","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-struktur","content":"Large document batches arrive with data locked in semi-structured text. Invoices need to flow into spreadsheets. Product datasheets need to become database rows. The tooling exists, but the orchestration overhead is disproportionate to the extraction task itself."},"1196":{"id":"/docs-20","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-struktur","content":"Managed APIs charge per page, impose schema constraints, and require document uploads to external infrastructure. LLM SDKs provide raw model access but leave you to write chunking, validation, retries, and merging every time."},"1197":{"id":"/docs-21","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-struktur","content":"Struktur fills the gap: a focused extraction engine with an **autonomous agent** that handles the orchestration so you can focus on the output."},"1198":{"id":"/docs-22","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-an-agent","content":"Traditional extraction strategies (simple, parallel, sequential) require you to choose the right approach upfront. The agent decides:"},"1199":{"id":"/docs-23","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-an-agent","content":"**When to read** — entire document or specific sections"},"1200":{"id":"/docs-24","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-an-agent","content":"**How to search** — grep for patterns, list directories, execute bash commands"},"1201":{"id":"/docs-25","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-an-agent","content":"**What to extract** — build output incrementally as it explores"},"1202":{"id":"/docs-26","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-an-agent","content":"**How to validate** — check against schema and retry automatically"},"1203":{"id":"/docs-27","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-an-agent","content":"The agent adapts to your document. Small invoices get read in one shot. Large catalogs get navigated systematically. The result is better accuracy without configuration complexity."},"1204":{"id":"/docs-28","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-managed-apis","content":"Limitation"},"1205":{"id":"/docs-29","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-managed-apis","content":"Impact"},"1206":{"id":"/docs-30","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-managed-apis","content":"Per-page pricing"},"1207":{"id":"/docs-31","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-managed-apis","content":"Does not scale for large batches"},"1208":{"id":"/docs-32","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-managed-apis","content":"Schema constraints"},"1209":{"id":"/docs-33","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-managed-apis","content":"You work within their data model"},"1210":{"id":"/docs-34","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-managed-apis","content":"Document upload"},"1211":{"id":"/docs-35","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-managed-apis","content":"Non-starter for confidential workloads"},"1212":{"id":"/docs-36","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-managed-apis","content":"Black-box behavior"},"1213":{"id":"/docs-37","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-managed-apis","content":"Debugging extraction failures is opaque"},"1214":{"id":"/docs-38","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-a-plain-llm-sdk-call","content":"A single `generateText()` call gives you:"},"1215":{"id":"/docs-39","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-a-plain-llm-sdk-call","content":"No chunking for large documents"},"1216":{"id":"/docs-40","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-a-plain-llm-sdk-call","content":"No retries on schema validation failure"},"1217":{"id":"/docs-41","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-a-plain-llm-sdk-call","content":"No merging of multi-chunk results"},"1218":{"id":"/docs-42","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-a-plain-llm-sdk-call","content":"No typed output inferred from your schema"},"1219":{"id":"/docs-43","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-not-a-plain-llm-sdk-call","content":"You write the same orchestration boilerplate every time. Struktur's agent packages that orchestration into a single, adaptive strategy."},"1220":{"id":"/docs-44","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#design-philosophy","content":"**Agent-first, zero configuration.** The agent strategy is the default. It explores documents autonomously, deciding when to read, search, or extract. No need to pick chunk sizes or parallelism upfront."},"1221":{"id":"/docs-45","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#design-philosophy","content":"**Autonomous exploration.** The agent uses a virtual filesystem to read files, grep for patterns, find files, and execute commands. It builds output incrementally as it discovers data."},"1222":{"id":"/docs-46","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#design-philosophy","content":"**Shell-composable by default.** Reads stdin, writes stdout, speaks JSON. Integrates with `jq`, `find`, `curl`, and any tool in your pipeline."},"1223":{"id":"/docs-47","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#design-philosophy","content":"**Validation in the loop.** Errors go back to the model, not to you. The retry loop means most extractions converge within two attempts."},"1224":{"id":"/docs-48","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#design-philosophy","content":"**Schema-first.** You define the shape, Struktur guarantees it."},"1225":{"id":"/docs-49","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#design-philosophy","content":"**Fields shorthand.** Skip the JSON Schema boilerplate with `--fields \"title, price:number, status:enum{draft|live}\"`."},"1226":{"id":"/docs-50","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#trade-offs","content":"Trade-off"},"1227":{"id":"/docs-51","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#trade-offs","content":"Rationale"},"1228":{"id":"/docs-52","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#trade-offs","content":"Requires tool-calling models"},"1229":{"id":"/docs-53","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#trade-offs","content":"The agent needs models that support function calling (Claude, GPT-4, etc.)"},"1230":{"id":"/docs-54","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#trade-offs","content":"Depends on Vercel AI SDK providers"},"1231":{"id":"/docs-55","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#trade-offs","content":"OpenAI, Anthropic, Google supported; self-hosted models need OpenAI-compatible API"},"1232":{"id":"/docs-56","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#trade-offs","content":"Token costs vary by document"},"1233":{"id":"/docs-57","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#trade-offs","content":"The agent makes multiple tool calls; large documents cost more than small ones"},"1234":{"id":"/docs-58","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#a-10-second-demo","content":"Expected output:"},"1235":{"id":"/docs-59","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#a-10-second-demo","content":"The agent reads the PDF, decides how to extract the fields, and returns validated JSON."},"1236":{"id":"/docs-60","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-struktur-is-not","content":"**It is not a general document conversion tool.** It parses files for extraction purposes, not for format conversion. It does not produce formatted output from documents."},"1237":{"id":"/docs-61","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-struktur-is-not","content":"**It is not a managed API.** It runs locally and calls your provider directly."},"1238":{"id":"/docs-62","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-struktur-is-not","content":"**It does not stream.** Input in, JSON out."},"1239":{"id":"/docs-63","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-struktur-is-not","content":"**It is not a general LLM orchestration framework.**"},"1240":{"id":"/docs-64","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-struktur-is-not","content":"For the full mental model, see The Extraction Pipeline."},"1241":{"id":"/docs-65","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#who-is-it-for","content":"<Card title=\"CLI Users\" description=\"Data engineers, analysts, shell pipeline builders — use Struktur for one-off extractions, batch processing, and CI/CD automation without writing code.\" />"},"1242":{"id":"/docs-66","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#who-is-it-for","content":"<Card title=\"SDK Users\" description=\"TypeScript developers embedding extraction in applications — use Struktur for typed results, custom strategies, and fine-grained control over the extraction pipeline.\" />"},"1243":{"id":"/docs-67","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-is-the-agent-strategy","content":"The agent strategy is the default and recommended way to use Struktur. It implements:"},"1244":{"id":"/docs-68","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-is-the-agent-strategy","content":"**Virtual filesystem tools** — read, grep, find, ls, bash"},"1245":{"id":"/docs-69","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-is-the-agent-strategy","content":"**Output management** — set\\_output\\_data, update\\_output\\_data, finish, fail"},"1246":{"id":"/docs-70","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-is-the-agent-strategy","content":"**Autonomous exploration** — the agent decides what to do based on your schema"},"1247":{"id":"/docs-71","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-is-the-agent-strategy","content":"**Incremental extraction** — builds output as it discovers data"},"1248":{"id":"/docs-72","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#how-it-works","content":"The agent receives your schema and access to a virtual filesystem containing the document"},"1249":{"id":"/docs-73","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#how-it-works","content":"It can read files, search for patterns, list directories, and execute commands"},"1250":{"id":"/docs-74","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#how-it-works","content":"As it finds data, it calls `set_output_data` or `update_output_data` to build the result"},"1251":{"id":"/docs-75","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#how-it-works","content":"When complete, it calls `finish` to return validated JSON"},"1252":{"id":"/docs-76","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#when-to-use-other-strategies","content":"The agent is the default and works best for most documents. However, other strategies are available for specific cases:"},"1253":{"id":"/docs-77","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#when-to-use-other-strategies","content":"Strategy"},"1254":{"id":"/docs-78","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],