tart-17","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#set-a-default-model-if-not-using---default","content":"Once set, `--model` is optional in all `extract` commands."},"1305":{"id":"/docs/quickstart-18","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#extract-your-first-data","content":"The `--fields` flag builds a JSON Schema on the fly. Each field defaults to `string`; append `:number`, `:integer`, `:bool`, etc. to set the type. See Fields Shorthand for the full syntax."},"1306":{"id":"/docs/quickstart-19","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#extract-your-first-data","content":"If you need more control (optional fields, nested objects), pass a full schema instead:"},"1307":{"id":"/docs/quickstart-20","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#extract-your-first-data","content":"Notice that `total` is a number, not a string — Struktur enforced the schema."},"1308":{"id":"/docs/quickstart-21","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#what-happened","content":"For the text example, stdin input was loaded as an artifact, the LLM generated output, and it was validated against your schema. The `simple` strategy handled this in a single LLM call."},"1309":{"id":"/docs/quickstart-22","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#what-happened","content":"For the PDF example, an extra step happened first: the built-in PDF parser extracted text (and optionally images) from the file and converted it into an artifact, then extraction proceeded as normal. Add `--images` to include embedded images, or `--screenshots` to render page screenshots."},"1310":{"id":"/docs/quickstart-23","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#what-happened","content":"To understand what happened inside, read The Extraction Pipeline."},"1311":{"id":"/docs/quickstart-