ing an **autonomous agent**. It turns documents into validated, schema-typed JSON by having an LLM agent explore the content, decide what to read, and build the output incrementally."],[813,"Struktur is built on the Vercel AI SDK, which provides a unified interface to multiple LLM providers. This architecture makes it straightforward to use any model from supported providers—or add new ones."],[63,"Struktur is published as an npm package and runs on Node.js 20 or newer. Install it in your image; there is no standalone binary to download."],[513,"Struktur only cares about what is in the artifact, not where it came from."],[1539,"Struktur provides an Agent Skill that teaches AI coding assistants (like Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, etc.) how to use Struktur effectively."],[842,"Struktur supports two authentication methods:"],[1161,"Struktur uses **lenient validation** during intermediate extraction steps:"],[586,"Struktur validates artifact JSON before processing. Use the CLI:"],[1794,"Struktur vs Alternatives"],[669,"Struktur's parser system converts files into Artifact format before any LLM work happens. Parsers are resolved by MIME type and are fully configurable."],[116,"Suffix"],[1555,"Support"],[771,"Supported input kinds:"],[801,"Supported Providers"],[114,"Supported providers: `openai`, `anthropic`, `google`, `cerebras`, `opencode`, `openrouter`, `ollama`."],[1536,"Supported Tools"],[3,"Synopsis"],[94,"Synopsis"],[174,"Synopsis"],[303,"Synopsis"],[392,"Synopsis"],[1422,"Target width in pixels (overrides `screenshotScale`)"],[465,"Test a schema against samples"],[1071,"Testing or prototyping"],[775,"Text artifact (split on double newlines)"],[1392,"Text artifact (split on double newlines)"],[553,"Text content of this slice"],[375,"Text content with expand/collapse per-slice (truncated at 500 chars, full text on click)"],[727,"Text is split on double newlines into content slices automatically."],[947,"The **Agent** strategy is the default and recommended way to use Struktur. It gives the LLM a virtual filesystem and lets it autonomously decide how to extract your data."],[1302,"The `--default` flag automatically queries the provider API and sets the cheapest available model as default, so `--model` becomes optional in all future commands."],[255,"The `--default` flag automatically queries the provider API and sets the cheapest available model as default. One command, fully ready."],[189,"The `--fields` flag (short: `-f`) lets you describe extraction output as a comma-separated string directly on the command line, without writing or maintaining a JSON Schema file."],[1305,"The `--fields` flag builds a JSON Schema on the fly. Each field defaults to `string`; append `:number`, `:integer`, `:bool`, etc. to set the type. See Fields Shorthand for the full syntax."],[207,"The `fields` parameter is also available in the SDK:"],[759,"The `FILE_PATH` placeholder is replaced with the actual file path at runtime. For buffer inputs, a temp file is created automatically."],[584,"The `imageType` field is set automatically by the PDF parser: `\"embedded\"` for images extracted from the PDF body (requires `--images`), `\"screenshot\"` for full-page renders (requires `--screenshots`) and for the generated image overview. The artifact viewer uses this field to filter and badge images independently."],[1388,"The `parse()` function is the primary way to load files and text into artifacts. It handles MIME detection, parser resolution, and PDF image extraction automatically."],[618,"The `simple` strategy loads all artifacts as-is. If the input exceeds the context window, the LLM call may fail or produce degraded results. For large inputs, use a chunked strategy."],[1014,"The agent adapts to your document:"],[1203,"The agent adapts to your document. Small invoices get read in one shot. Large catalogs get navigated systematically. The result is better accuracy without configuration complexity."],[1045,"The agent can:"],[1041,"The agent has access to a virtual filesystem containing:"],[1025,"The agent imposes two hard requirements that the other strategies do not:"],[1058,"The agent is encouraged to update output continuously as it explores, not wait until the end."],[1252,"The agent is the default and works best for most documents. However, other strategies are available for specific cases:"],[1233,"The agent makes multiple tool calls; large documents cost more than small ones"],[1229,"The agent needs models that support function calling (Claude, GPT-4, etc.)"],[1019,"The agent normally spends its first steps reading `/artifact.json` and looking at the image overview. Prefill hands it that context up front so it can extract immediately:"],[161,"The agent normally spends its first steps reading `/artifact.json` and viewing the image overview. Prefill hands it that context up front, as completed `read` and `view_image` tool calls, so it can start extracting immediately:"],[1235,"The agent reads the PDF, decides how to extract the fields, and returns validated JSON."],[1248,"The agent receives your schema and access to a virtual filesystem containing the document"],[1609,"The agent should confirm it can see the skill and describe what it knows about Struktur."],[1243,"The agent strategy is the default and recommended way to use Struktur. It implements:"],[883,"The agent strategy queries the provider's model catalogue for the input modalities a model accepts and enables image tools only when `image` is present. If the catalogue cannot be reached, or reports nothing for the model, vision is left **enabled** — the extraction fails loudly at the provider instead of silently running text-only. Override the detection explicitly with the agent strategy's `vision: false` option."],[913,"The Agent strategy uses autonomous exploration. Other strategies are available for specific use cases."],[1636,"The agent will recognize these requests and load the skill automatically."],[1726,"The agent:"],[1031,"The agent's whole loop